# Build-context exclusions for BOTH images.
#
# This file must live at the repo root. Both services build with `context: .`,
# and Docker only reads the .dockerignore at the context root — per-app
# .dockerignore files are silently ignored in that setup. That mistake copied
# kprime-backend/node_modules into the backend image (324 MB -> 1.68 GB) and
# made the storefront build fail outright, because the host's pnpm symlink tree
# collided with the one installed inside the image.

# Dependency trees — reinstalled inside each image for the right platform.
**/node_modules

# Build output — regenerated inside the image.
**/.next
**/.medusa
**/dist
**/out

# 777 generated placeholder PNGs (~19 MB). Regenerated on the server into a
# mounted volume; demo data never belongs baked into an image.
kprime-backend/static

# Secrets. Containers get their environment from compose at runtime.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Test artefacts and local noise.
**/test-results
**/playwright-report
**/coverage
**/*.log
.git
.github
**/.DS_Store
